message: "If you use this software or data, please cite the following reference(s)."
title: "A Typed Certification Protocol for Finite-State Causal Abstractions"
abstract: "Coarse-grained dynamics can be well defined while failing to preserve the targets or persistence events that motivate a model. This paper presents a typed certification protocol for finite-state, discrete-time controlled Markov systems. The protocol separates state aggregation, action implementation, history-response equivalence, and event-order quotients, and records their assumptions within a fixed task contract. This record has not been peer-reviewed."
